+++ b/wire_ui_builder_v0.12-dev2-readiness/ROW_COLLECTIONS.md
@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+# Authoritative row collections — v0.12-dev1
+
+`WireUIRowCollectionContract` makes the common 0/1/N list/table/worklist shape a compiled Builder contract rather than application JavaScript convention.
+
+The minimum authored shape is:
+
+- `collectionSlot` — the authoritative row collection slot;
+- `countSlot` — optional but recommended explicit authoritative count slot;
+- `identityField` — required stable semantic row identity, never a visible row position;
+- `rowFields` — explicit display/order fields;
+- `selectionMode` — `NONE`, `SINGLE` or `MULTI`;
+- optional `selectedIdsSlot` and `workspaceContextSlot`;
+- `emptyPolicy` — `ALLOW_EMPTY` or `FAIL_CLOSED`;
+- optional filter and sort field allow-lists;
+- optional row / selection / filter / sort semantic action names.
+
+The Builder Studio projection editor exposes these directly. A designer does not author a browser loop or a DOM row template. The compiled immutable definition carries `rowContract` alongside the ordinary semantic element/component/projection references.
+
+## Authority rules
+
+This contract is presentation/authorship metadata, not application authority.
+
+- The row identity comes from the server-owned object identity field.
+- Row order is presentation only.
+- A renderer must never infer semantic identity from position.
+- Filters and sorts emit semantic intent; they do not locally redefine the authoritative result population.
+- Selection is represented by semantic IDs.
+- `workspaceContext` is carried unchanged to actions when supplied by Wire UI Server v0.17.
+- Query/scope/order/selection/result revision validation remains a Wire UI Server/application responsibility.
+- Business row fields are never echoed back as transaction authority merely because they were displayed.
+
+## Fail-closed rendering
+
+When `countSlot` is present and `emptyPolicy=FAIL_CLOSED`, a collection/count mismatch does not silently display zero rows or enable a misleading row action. Missing/duplicate semantic identities are also invalid.
+
+This directly addresses the class of failure exposed by FlyLo where one value had been treated both as a passenger collection and a passenger count.
+
+## Federation-company baseline
+
+Use this model for operational worklists, customer/passenger lists, policy/case lists, books/trades, staff/merchant rows and other Federation-company UIs. Application-specific presentation may vary, but semantic row identity, explicit count, filtering/sorting authority and stale-context rejection must not.
